ve system.", "PANCREATIC NEUROENDOCRINE TUMORS:Pancreatic neuroendocrine tumors are a specific type of neuroendocrine tumor that occurs in the pancreas, which can be functional or non-functional and vary in their clinical behavior.", "ADENOCARCINOMA:Adenocarcinoma is a type of cancer that forms in mucus-secreting glands and can be a component of neuroendocrine tumors, particularly in mixed neoplasms.", "CARCINOMA DE CÉLULAS EN ANILLO DE SELLO:Ring cell carcinoma is a rare type of cancer characterized by ring-shaped cells and can be associated with neuroendocrine tumors.", "CÁNCER DE CÉLULAS ESCAMOSAS:Squamous cell carcinoma is a type of cancer that arises from squamous cells and can also be a component of mixed neuroendocrine neoplasms.", "ÍNDICE DE PROLIFERACIÓN KI-67:The Ki-67 proliferation index is a marker used to determine the growth fraction of a given cell population, particularly in the context of neuroendocrine tumors.", "ÍNDICE MITÓTICO:The mitotic index is a measure of the number of cells undergoing mitosis in a given population, which is important for assessing the aggressiveness of tumors, including neuroendocrine tumors.", "NEUROENDOCRINE TUMORS:", "SOMATOSTATINOMAS:Somatostatinomas are rare tumors that occur in the pancreas and duodenum, often associated with various syndromes and conditions.", "DUODENUM:The duodenum is the first part of the small intestine where somatostatinomas can also occur.", "NEUROFIBROMATOSIS TYPE 1:Neurofibromatosis type 1 is a genetic disorder that can be associated with duodenal tumors.", "VON HIPPEL-LINDAU SYNDROME:Von Hippel-Lindau syndrome is a genetic condition that can be associated with duodenal tumors.", "MEN1 SYNDROME:MEN1 syndrome is a hereditary condition that can lead to the development of pancreatic neuroendocrine tumors."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}